# Look at the model before you hand it over

A generation that returned a GLB URL has not necessarily produced the right model.
After `forge_free`, `mesh_forge`, `text_to_avatar`, `forge_avatar`, `refine_model` or
`rig_mesh` returns a model:

1. Call `look_at_model` with the returned `glb_url`. It renders the model from several
   angles and returns the frames as images you can see.
2. Compare the frames with what the user asked for: the right object, the right
   colors and materials, nothing missing or fused, a humanoid standing upright when a
   rigged character was requested.
3. If it is wrong, say what is wrong and fix it with `refine_model` ("make the handle
   longer", "brass, not silver"), then look again. Do not claim a model matches the
   request without having rendered it.
4. Hand over the GLB URL and the viewer link together with one sentence on what the
   render shows.

If a generation answered `pending`, collect it with `check_job` (or `get_job`) first;
only a finished job has a GLB to look at.
